+ * With SPP_PMTUD_DISABLE, write only net->mtu -- the ceiling on packet size --
+ * and leave asoc->smallest_mtu, which drives message fragmentation, alone.
+ *
+ * For path MTU discovery (RFC 8899): a probe needs to emit a packet larger than
+ * the confirmed path MTU, and the output path caps packets at net->mtu, so the
+ * ceiling has to move. Fragmentation must *not*, or user messages would be split
+ * for a size nothing has acknowledged yet and a failed probe would cost
+ * retransmissions instead of just the probe.
+ */
+#define SPP_PACKET_CEILING_ONLY 0x00000400
